      "claim": "All L1 gold-voting contexts report absolute oral bioavailability values well above the 20% threshold: safinamide ~95%, rufinamide ≈85%, alfuzosin 49%, bumetanide 74.8%, trovafloxacin 87.6%, lemborexant ≥87%, ketanserin 49.3–60%, diclofenac ≈50%, and meloxicam 91%; no gold context provides an affirmative F<20% outcome.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C03","C04","C05","C06","C07","C08","C09","C10","C11","C12","C13","C14","C15","C16","C17"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 records reinforce these high-F outcomes and provide no affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C18","C19","C20","C22","C23","C24","C25","C26","C27","C28","C29","C30","C32","C33","C34","C35","C36","C37","C38","C39","C40","C41","C42","C43"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for structurally related 2,4-diaminopyrimidines (tetroxoprim, trimethoprim), rufinamide, and retigabine show measurable systemic exposure after oral dosing, consistent with absorption sufficient to support F≥20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C45","C50","C51","C54","C55","C59","C70","C85","C90"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 includes positive absorption records for aminoheterocycle ester/carbonate prodrugs that were well absorbed after oral administration in mice, supporting the absorption component of the query's diaminopyrimidine-like core.",
      "card_ids": ["C98","C100","C131"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 also includes a high Caco-2 A→B permeability value, but for a structurally distant analog; it provides only weak supportive context.",
      "card_ids": ["C117"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 low-solubility records for carbamate heteroaromatics (mebendazole, flubendazole, albendazole, oxfendazole) and aminoquinazolines (prazosin, doxazosin), plus one explicit link of poor solubility to variable oral bioavailability, are absorption risk factors; none affirmatively establishes F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C95","C103","C105","C112","C118","C121","C127","C136"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L4 record provides a transferable direct low-F outcome; low solubility and high TPSA are uncertainties, not affirmative evidence for F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C118","C121"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
