      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "weakened",
      "card_ids": ["C95","C103","C105","C112","C118","C121","C127","C136"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific absolute oral bioavailability or matched oral/IV PK measurement is available; prediction relies on transfer from training contexts and analog records.",
    "No query-specific solubility or permeability measurement is available; L4 records are for analogs with varying structural similarity and formulation context.",
    "Low solubility of carbamate heteroaromatics is a risk factor, but dose and formulation for the query are unspecified, so solubility alone cannot establish F<20%.",
    "High TPSA (146.86), HBA count (9), and possible first-pass/carbamate or aniline metabolism remain uncharacterized; no efflux or intestinal metabolism data are available at this level.",
    "L4 records are non-gold context; they inform the absorption component but do not add independent gold votes."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L4 adds mostly solubility data for carbamate/aminoheterocycle analogs; low solubility is a risk but no record affirmatively shows F<20%, while positive mouse absorption records for aminoheterocycle prodrugs support the absorption component. The uniformly high L1/L2 gold outcomes and measurable L3 oral exposure for related scaffolds remain decisive, so prediction stays high with moderate confidence."
}

